course: dictionary
lesson: 13622
title: Indispensable
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Indispensable is a long word, but you can break it into parts. The start, in-, means not. Dispensable means something you can do without. So indispensable means something you cannot do without.
explain: Look at the words around it: «Our torch is indispensable on camping trips, because the nights are very dark.» The clue is that the torch is needed when it is dark. So indispensable means so useful that you really need it.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Water is indispensable for plants.» Could you say water is not needed for plants? No, so indispensable fits. Look out for the phrases indispensable to, indispensable for, and an indispensable tool.
fact: Indispensable means so important or useful that you cannot manage without it.
fact: An indispensable person is someone a team or group really needs.
fact: Indispensable is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «an indispensable tool».
fact: «Indispensable to» and «indispensable for» are common phrases: «Good sleep is indispensable for growing children.»
fact: Adverts and formal writing often use indispensable to show that something is necessary.
exercise: «A map is indispensable when you are lost in a new city.» What does indispensable mean here? | Hard to read | Cheap to buy | Very colourful | *So useful you cannot manage without it
exercise: «Our class captain is indispensable to the team.» What does this sentence tell us? | *The team really needs her | She is tired every day | She is the smallest in the team | The team does not need her at all
exercise: Which word means you cannot manage without it? | ordinary | sudden | pleasant | *indispensable
test: «A good pair of boots is indispensable on a muddy hill walk.» What does indispensable mean? | Old and worn | Very muddy | Cheap | *Needed, so you cannot manage without them
test: Which sentence shows that something is really needed? | We played indispensable games at break | The cake was indispensable and sweet | The sky is indispensable and blue | *Oxygen is indispensable to every living thing
exam: Jayden says indispensable means very cheap. What is the real meaning? | *So important you cannot manage without it | Easy to break | Very cheap and easy to find | Very small and light
